	This block is deliberately NOT part of the metadata comment above (#452).

	The manifest fingerprint drops a leading comment that carries a `name:`
	line, because `usage:` and `category:` are per-project and regenerated
	downstream (#227). A fixture's Run: and Expected: lines are the opposite —
	skeleton-owned, and the only thing carrying the fixture's claim to truth.
	Kept inside that block, an upstream rewrite is invisible to drift
	detection: downstream keeps the old wording, verify reports OK, and
	fixtures.spec.js then fails on a fixture it cannot parse.
	Measured on eprukaz, 2026-07-30.
#}
{#
TemplateOrderRule fixture — OK case.

Component template that follows the canonical top-level order:
